  "summary": "Menlo Park PD inadvertently allowed Houston PD and Sauk Village (IL) PD access to its Flock ALPR data, in violation of California law prohibiting sharing with out-of-state agencies. The department did not disclose the breach until questioned by The Almanac, did not include it in its quarterly council report, and refused a PRA request for search logs. The article also notes the city's online ALPR policy was never updated to reflect 2024 changes.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Although state law and Menlo Park policy forbid sharing ALPR data with out-of-state agencies, access to the city's system was shared with departments in both Illinois and Texas.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "During the period in which Houston had access to Menlo Park's system, Houston sent tens of thousands of requests that queried Menlo Park's database.",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    },
    {
      "quote": "State law explicitly prohibits the sharing of ALPR information with out-of-state or federal agencies. And the Attorney General confirmed that again in 2023 guidance",
      "paragraph_idx": 23
    },
    {
      "quote": "Menlo Park refused to provide the reports claiming that it would cause the city to generate new records",
      "paragraph_idx": 33
    }
  ],
